We are looking for experienced Ground Engineers B1 or B2. Are you up for this great opportunity?

After working hard with your team to deliver a Boeing 787 to your customer in perfect condition, you wave it off with pride. On to the next team challenge: solve a complicated avionic task on the Boeing 777 that has just rolled in! Or a P-inspection at Schiphol Centre while your colleague is doing the Software load. 

Tasks & responsibilities
Ensuring (maintenance) processes on the ground run flawlessly;
Perform inspection, maintenance and modification acitvities and supervise them professionally;
Carry out the work according to the required specifications and in compliance with the various regulations (such as those from the Safety Management System);
Release aircraft to service by means of a Certificate of Release to Service which, in your opinion, are suitable for safe flight operations;
Improve the current maintenance processes structurally and proactively;
Contribute to the further development of your team.

What else will you bring with you?
Demonstrable relevant work experience as (EASA) licensed Ground Engineer for one or more of the following aircraft types B737, B777, A330, A320 NEO and/or B787 (A dossier/document check is part of the selection process);
Good (technical) English, both spoken and written, is a must;
Good Dutch, both spoken and written, is an advantage
Experience working in a team is a plus.

The world is at your feet as a certified engine mechanic. You maintain, overhaul, and modify aircraft engines and individual components. It's also your responsibility to certify them. With your experience, you serve as a role model for junior engine mechanics.

You test the engine for internal damage and detect any anomalies;• You work with various engine types;• You always keep the customer’s requirements in mind;• You report daily to the team lead and the lead mechanic of the Engine Shop;• You perform administrative tasks;• You adhere to safety regulations.

You’ll be part of Engine Services, a division of Engineering & Maintenance (E&M) where you’ll work in the Maintenance, Repair & Overhaul (MRO) department. You will work in shifts: one week of day shifts and one week of evening shifts.

You’re a real techie and love working with your hands. You work quickly but precisely, always spotting potential errors immediately. You also have a strong sense of responsibility and find it important that you and your team can work safely. You don’t hesitate to address colleagues if they don’t follow the regulations. Additionally, you enjoy sharing your experience with junior engine mechanics and helping them find their way in the department.

Furthermore:
You are authorized to perform maintenance on aircraft engines;
You can work independently and sign off on completed work;
You speak and understand (technical) English well;
You have at least three years of experience as an engine mechanic;
You are familiar with engine types CFM56-7B, CF6, GEnx, and LEAP.

Are you looking for a stable full-time job in logistics where you can combine working with a reach truck with a variety of warehouse activities? Do you enjoy a hands-on role, work accurately, and feel comfortable in an international team? Then this Warehouse Operative position could be a great next step for you.

You will work in a modern distribution centre in Hazeldonk, where you will operate a reach truck but also be involved in picking, packing, loading, unloading, and other warehouse activities. You will work in both English and Dutch and have the opportunity to build a long-term career in logistics.

What are you going to do?
As a Warehouse Operative, you play an important role in the daily warehouse operation. You will use your reach truck certificate to safely move and store goods, but your work will involve much more than operating a reach truck. Together with your colleagues, you make sure incoming and outgoing goods are processed accurately and efficiently.

Key Responsibilities:

- Operating a reach truck to move, store, and retrieve goods safely;
- Picking, packing, and preparing customer orders for dispatch;
- Loading and unloading goods and checking incoming shipments;
- Performing quality checks and verifying product quantities and accuracy;
- Carrying out various physical warehouse activities, including lifting and moving packages of approximately 20–30 kg;
- Supporting colleagues with other logistics activities when needed.

Working Hours:

- Monday to Friday;
- Day shift;
- Full-time position of 40 hours per week.

What do we offer?
You will join a professional international logistics environment where you can use your reach truck experience while gaining experience across different warehouse activities. The company offers a stable working environment and opportunities to develop within logistics.

Besides this, you will receive:

- Gross hourly salary of €14.99;
- Full-time employment of 40 hours per week;
- Long-term employment opportunities;

(Administrative) logistics employee (2-shifts) 
 Logistiek en Supply chain Administratief en Secretarieel 36 - 40 uur 2500 - 3000 EUR 3000 - 3500 EUR 
 Introduction You do not let a single pallet go through without having seen it. It does not go into the warehouse until you have put the sticker on it. 
 What are you going to do? 
You are the one where the inbound process starts. Once the container is at the dock, you will check if it is the right one. Furthermore, you will 
Check the weight, length and width of the article; 
Check that all items are present in the container; 
Communicate deviations when they occur to your coordinator; 
You adjust deviations, with permission from your supervisor; 
Helps stack pallets; 
Check full pallets, drive them away with an EPT and make sure they are sealed. 
You also ensure that your team is and remains motivated; together we are strong! 
 This is what you get in return! 
We offer a competitive salary of 15,47€ per hour excluding 12,5% shift allowance. 
You can start right away and if everything goes well, more options could be available. 
 This is you! 
Do you have a positive attitude; 
Your communication skills are on point; 
Do you know how to carry out proper checks; 
Do you have experience as a logistics employee; 
Are you fluent in English; 
Do you get excited about working two shifts; 
Do you have an EPT certificate or are willing to get one; 
In addition to English and Dutch, do you also speak Polish? Then do not hold back and respond! 
 Here's where you'll get to work: Our client is one of the biggest retail suppliers in Europe. They are a regional giant with countless opportunities. 
